    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/317195": {
      "title": "Anatomic Pathologist, Pathology & Laboratory Medicine, Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine",
      "description": "Anatomic Pathologist, Pathology & Laboratory Medicine, Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Anatomic Pathologist, Pathology & Laboratory Medicine, Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Anatomic Pathologist, Pathology & Laboratory Medicine, Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937590821 Posted Date 8/21/2026 Minimum Salary $240,951.00 Maximum Salary $427,772.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular ANATOMIC PATHOLOGIST, BOSTON, MASSACHUSETTS (USA), with surgical pathology and/or cytopathology and other subspecialty fellowship training preferred. The Department of Pathology & Laboratory Medicine at Boston Medical Center Health System and Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine is recruiting a full-time AP board certified/eligible Pathologist who has strong general pathology and other subspecialty skills. The ideal candidate will have a demonstrated interest in teaching pathology residents, medical and graduate students. There is an expectation of scholarly activity including collaborative research and publications, but the candidate will not be expected to submit grants for extramural funding. Academic rank will depend on the credentials of the applicant. Boston Medical Center was formed by the merger of the historic Boston City Hospital and Boston University Hospital in 1996. We are a non-profit 496 bed academic medical center located in the South End of Boston. The Department of Pathology & Laboratory Medicine has 37 faculty who engage in clinical service, education and research. More information about the Department may be found on our websites: http://www.bumc.bu.edu/busm-pathology/ & https://www.bmc.org/medical-professionals/pathology-laboratory-medicine Boston University and Boston Medical Center Health System are equal opportunity, affirmative action employers. Candidates underrepresented in medicine and science are encouraged to apply. The Department of Pathology & Laboratory Medicine strongly believes that the cultural and social diversity of our faculty, staff and students is vitally important to the distinction and excellence of our clinical, research and academic programs. As a department and institution we embrace and champion equity, diversity and inclusion. The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training, and departmental budget. The salary range is $240,951 to $427,772. The above hiring range represents a good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. BU conducts a background check on all final candidates for certain faculty and staff positions. The background check includes contacting the final candidate’s current and previous employer(s) to ask whether, in the last seven years, there has been a substantiated finding of misconduct violating that employer’s applicable sexual misconduct policies. To implement this process, the University requires a final candidate to complete and sign the form entitled “Authorization to Release Information” after execution of an offer letter. Required Skills Surgical pathology and/or cytopathology and other subspecialty fellowship training preferred. AP board certified/eligible Pathologist who has strong general pathology and other subspecialty skills. Application Instructions: Please send a cover letter and current curriculum vitae to: Christopher Andry, MPhil, PhD Professor & Chair, Department of Pathology & Laboratory Medicine Boston Medical Center Health System & Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine 670 Albany Street, room 407 Boston MA 02118 617-358-2929 Chris.Andry@bmc.org This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/316637": {
      "title": "Board-Eligible or Board-Certified Pediatric Endocrinologist, Pediatrics Department, Boston Medical Center",
      "description": "Board-Eligible or Board-Certified Pediatric Endocrinologist, Pediatrics Department, Boston Medical Center - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Board-Eligible or Board-Certified Pediatric Endocrinologist, Pediatrics Department, Boston Medical Center - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Board-Eligible or Board-Certified Pediatric Endocrinologist, Pediatrics Department, Boston Medical Center ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937220423 Posted Date 8/10/2026 Minimum Salary $180,000.00 Maximum Salary $250,000.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Overview The Department of Pediatrics at Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine and Boston Medical Center (BMC) is seeking a Board-Eligible or Board-Certified Pediatric Endocrinologist who is passionate about clinical care, teaching, and program development to join our Division of Endocrinology. About the Position Boston Medical Center (BMC) Pediatrics is a national leader in advancing health equity for children The successful candidate will join a multidisciplinary team that includes endocrine nurse, nutritionist, PharmD and NP. How to Apply: Send your CV and a letter of interest to pediatricsfacultyaffairs@bmc.org with the subject line: “BMC Pediatric Endocrinologist\". Required Skills Responsibilities include: Ambulatory pediatric endocrinology care Inpatient consultative services Teaching and supervision of medical students and pediatric residents Opportunities for collaboration with the Division of Adult Endocrinology Participation in program development, quality improvement, and clinical scholarship This position offers a unique opportunity to play a meaningful role in the growth and strategic direction of pediatric endocrinology and diabetes care within the Department of Pediatrics. We are especially interested in candidates with strong clinical skills, a commitment to caring for medically and socially complex patients, and an interest in practicing in a mission-driven academic environment. Compensation: Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine (BU-CASM) offers a competitive salary commensurate with academic training and practice experience. We continue to evaluate our compensation plan to remain one of the most competitive in salary and benefits. Our staff receive a highly competitive salary and generous benefits that include paid vacation, sick time, parental leave, and CME expenses. Faculty members and their dependents qualify for greatly reduced tuition at Boston University, ranked among the top 50 universities in the US. Compensation ranges between $180,000 and $ 250,000 Equal Opportunity Statement We are an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. We believe the cultural and social diversity of our faculty, staff, and learners is vital to the excellence of our clinical, research, and academic missions. BU conducts a background check on all final candidates for certain faculty and staff positions. The background check includes contacting the final candidate’s current and previous employer(s) to ask whether, in the last seven years, there has been a substantiated finding of misconduct violating that employer’s applicable sexual misconduct policies. To implement this process, the University requires a final candidate to complete and sign the form entitled “Authorization to Release Information” after execution of an offer letter This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/317245": {
      "title": "Cancer Genetics Clinical Director, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology",
      "description": "Cancer Genetics Clinical Director, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Cancer Genetics Clinical Director, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Cancer Genetics Clinical Director, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937630903 Posted Date 9/3/2026 Minimum Salary $255,670.00 Maximum Salary $534,220.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Section of Hematology & Oncology at Boston Medical Center (BMC) and Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine are seeking a medical oncologist/hematologist as Cancer Genetics Clinical Director to provide physician leadership and clinical oversight for the Cancer Genetics Program and High-Risk Genetics Clinic. The Director will partner closely with a multi-disciplinary team and ambulatory leadership as a member of the Section of Hematology & Oncology to ensure the delivery of high-quality, evidence-based hereditary cancer risk assessment, genetic testing, and surveillance for patients referred. The Director will provide clinical and operational leadership for the program and supervise a team of Genetic Counselors (GCs). Candidates will provide consultation and follow up to patients referred to the High-Risk Genetics clinic as well as a patient panel with hematologic and/or oncologic disorders in the specialty of their choosing. Key Responsibilities Clinical Leadership & Genetic Counselor Oversight Provide physician leadership and clinical oversight for a team of Genetic Counselors and the High- Risk Genetics Program. Provide consultation and clinical guidance for complex, atypical, or discordant genetic testing results. Provide expertise regarding hereditary cancer syndromes and testing. High-Risk Cancer Clinic Lead weekly multidisciplinary High-Risk Cancer Clinic conference and provide physician input on complex cases. See patients in consultation and follow up referred to the High-Risk Cancer Clinic. Review patients with pathogenic or likely pathogenic variants, significant family histories, and elevated lifetime cancer risk. Guide screening, surveillance, and management recommendations using current evidence and nationally recognized guidelines Work in a multi-disciplinary team to facilitate appropriate advanced screening for patients followed in high-risk clinic Program Operations & Development Participate in monthly Cancer Genetics Operations meetings with Genetic Counseling and ambulatory leadership to optimize clinical operations, standardize work flow and promote quality safety and regulatory compliance. Education, Outreach & Collaboration Serve as a physician resource regarding germline testing, hereditary cancer risk, and complex genetic findings. Partner with the Genetic Counseling team to provide education to physicians, advanced practice providers, trainees and other referring clinicians. Lead and support community outreach to increase awareness of hereditary cancer risk, appropriate genetic testing, and referral pathways to the Hematology & Oncology Cancer Genetics Program. Promote multidisciplinary collaboration and continued growth of the Cancer Genetics and High-Risk Cancer programs. Hematology & Oncology Faculty Participate fully as a hematologist/oncologist physician in the Section of Hematology & Oncology including patient care, education and research missions. Commitment to provide primary specialty care to a panel of hematology/oncology patients in addition to the high-risk genetics clinic. Maintain an active Hematology/Medical Oncology practice with an independent panel of patients outside of the Cancer Genetics and High-Risk Clinic, in addition to providing clinical care and leadership for patients seen within the Cancer Genetics program. Required Skills MD or equivalent medical degree required. Board Eligible or Board Certified in Medical Oncology required; Board Eligibility or Board Certification in Hematology preferred. Licensed or eligible for medical licensure in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts. Clinical experience in cancer genetics, hereditary cancer syndromes, or a closely related field strongly preferred. Demonstrated ability to lead multidisciplinary clinical programs and collaborate effectively. Commitment to patient-centered care, health equity, education, and the academic missions of Boston Medical Center and Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine. To Apply: Interested candidates should send application materials (resume/CV and cover letter) to Casaundra Knight at Casaundra.Knight@bmc.org. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/316977": {
      "title": "Gastrointestinal Oncologist, School of Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology",
      "description": "Gastrointestinal Oncologist, School of Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Gastrointestinal Oncologist, School of Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Gastrointestinal Oncologist, School of Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937490706 Posted Date 7/6/2026 Minimum Salary $255,670.00 Maximum Salary $534,220.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology at Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine and Boston Medical Center is seeking a Gastrointestinal (GI) Oncologist. This rapidly expanding, multi-disciplinary program is focused on providing exceptional clinical care and performing high-impact research in GI oncology. The ideal candidate will have strong clinical expertise in GI medical oncology and a track record of collaboration in a multi-disciplinary care team. Opportunities within the program include participation in and leadership in clinical trials and collaborations with investigators pursuing a range of basic, translational, and health care delivery research projects. The successful candidate will also engage in teaching students, residents, and fellows in ambulatory and inpatient settings. Opportunities for leadership in medical education are also available. Required Skills Qualified candidates will possess an MD, DO or MD/PhD and be BC/BE in Medical Oncology. BE/BC in Hematology and Oncology preferred. Candidates will be licensed or eligible for a medical license in the state of Massachusetts. Academic rank will be based on qualifications and experience. How should candidates apply? Interested candidates should submit a letter of interest and CV to Casaundra Knight: casaundra.knight@bmc.org We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
