    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/317189": {
      "title": "Inpatient Hospitalist, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology",
      "description": "Inpatient Hospitalist, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Inpatient Hospitalist, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Inpatient Hospitalist, Medicine, Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937580819 Posted Date 8/19/2026 Minimum Salary $255,670.00 Maximum Salary $534,220.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Section of Hematology and Medical Oncology at Boston Medical Center and Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine, seeks an outstanding clinician to serve as a hospitalist on the inpatient hematology/oncology teaching service. The successful candidate must be board certified/eligible in internal medicine; additional certification in hematology/oncology is helpful but not required. The hospitalist will serve as an attending physician on the inpatient hematology/oncology service at Boston Medical Center, the major teaching hospital for Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine. They will rotate on the service for 36 weeks over the course of a year, supervising either a 10-patient or 16-patient team, in an alternating schedule. Both teams function as teaching services, and are staffed by residents and interns from the Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine internal medicine residency program. The hospitalist will serve as the service attending Monday-Friday. Weekend duties will be shared with other faculty in the section of hematology/oncology throughout the course of the year. Academic rank as Instructor or Assistant Professor of Medicine at Boston University Chobanian & Avedisian School of Medicine will be commensurate with experience, training, and achievements. Extensive collaborative opportunities with multiple disciplines provide an outstanding environment for research initiatives aimed at improving patient outcomes/safety, optimizing efficiency of patient progression through hospitalization, implementing new systems and processes, and establishing more consistent standards of practice in the acute care setting. The hospitalist will also participate in the education of medical students and the didactic training of residents. Required Skills Required credentials include an M.D., D.O. or M.D. /Ph.D. ABIM Board certification/board eligible in internal medicine Demonstrated interest and ability to provide acute care to hospitalized oncology patients. Work collaboratively in multi-disciplinary care teams Qualified candidates must be licensed or able to obtain a license in the State of Massachusetts. Qualified candidates must have legal authorization to work in the United States. Current BLS is required. Passion and interest for excellence in patient care and teaching in an academic inpatient hospital setting, with an interest in hematology/oncology. Application Instructions: Interested candidates should send application materials (resume/CV and cover letter) to Casaundra Knight at Casaundra.Knight@bmc.org. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/317322": {
      "title": "Part-Time Child Protection Team Pediatrician / Family Medicine Physician / Advanced Practice Nurse, Pediatrics, Boston Medical Center",
      "description": "Part-Time Child Protection Team Pediatrician / Family Medicine Physician / Advanced Practice Nurse, Pediatrics, Boston Medical Center - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Part-Time Child Protection Team Pediatrician / Family Medicine Physician / Advanced Practice Nurse, Pediatrics, Boston Medical Center - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Part-Time Child Protection Team Pediatrician / Family Medicine Physician / Advanced Practice Nurse, Pediatrics, Boston Medical Center ﻿ Category Boston University Medical Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937760921 Posted Date 9/21/2026 Minimum Salary $90,039.00 Maximum Salary $150,580.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Part-Time The Department of Pediatrics at the Boston University School of Medicine (BUSM) and Boston Medical Center (BMC) seek a Pediatrician, Family Medicine Physician, or Advanced Practice Nurse to join the BMC Child Protection Team. The Child Protection Team is a multidisciplinary team that covers all patients at BMC and provides consultation for BMC Health Systems hospitals and affiliated community health centers. The position involves the full scope of child maltreatment, including evaluation of patients in the emergency department, inpatient, and outpatient settings at Boston Medical Center as well as evaluation of patients in Foster Care Clinic and Child Protection Team outpatient clinic. Phone consultation provided to members of the multidisciplinary team throughout the BMC Health System and affiliated health centers. Teaching responsibilities include medical students, residents, and other learners in other programs at Boston Medical Center. Required Skills We employ a co-leadership model with parity between physician and social work members. Our multidisciplinary team strives to address child maltreatment using a diversity-, trauma-, and justice-informed approach. We encourage applicants with a passion for understanding the ways in which systems of oppression impact us, our patients, and our work. Applicants should have clinical expertise serving patients and families impacted by trauma, family disruption, and carceral systems; experience advocating for systems-based change is desired. Our multidisciplinary, collaborative approach seeks to encourage thoughtful and deliberative decision-making that centers patient and family well-being. Candidates with BC/BE in Child Abuse Pediatrics are preferred. Physician candidates (MD/DO) must be BC/BE in Pediatrics and must have or be eligible for a Massachusetts medical license. Highly qualified Advanced Practice Nurses will be considered. Fluency in languages other than English is highly desirable, but not required. Preference for candidates whose approach to child maltreatment is consonant with the framework outlined above. This is an 0.5 FTE position. For the remainder of effort required for additional clinical FTE, opportunities in pediatrics or other clinical departments may also be available. The appropriate series and appointment at the Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor level in the Clinical series will be determined based on the background and qualifications. To Apply: If interested in this employment opportunity, please send your resume/CV and cover letter directly to: PediatricsFacultyAffairs@bmc.org. We are an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, natural or protective hairstyle, religion, sex, age, national origin, physical or mental disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, military service, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, or because of marital, parental, or veteran status. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/317272": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Boston University School of Law",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Boston University School of Law - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Boston University School of Law - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Boston University School of Law ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937670910 Posted Date 9/10/2026 Minimum Salary $100,000.00 Maximum Salary $150,000.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Boston University invites applications for a non-tenure-track full-time Lecture or Senior Lecturer. Boston University School of Law invites applications from both entry-level and experienced candidates for a non-tenure-track full-time podium Lecturer with a projected start date of July 1, 2027. This position is primarily a teaching position. There is no expectation that this faculty member will produce scholarship. The search is broad and not limited to particular subjects, but we have especially strong teaching needs in American Indian Law, Contracts, Criminal Law, Criminal Procedure (both Investigatory and Adjudicatory), Evidence, Islamic Law, Professional Responsibility, Property, LGBTQ+ Rights and the Law, and Trust and Estates. The course load is 3-3, and the candidate should be open to other courses as needed. If appropriate, the person in this position may qualify for a Senior Lecturer position and might be eligible for a presumptively renewable contract after the required probationary period. Since its founding in 1839, Boston University has embraced a mission of openness and access, becoming one of the ﬁrst universities in the nation to welcome all students of ability regardless of race, gender, or creed. That tradition shapes our enduring commitment to academic freedom, free inquiry, and the robust exchange of ideas. Please visit https://www.bu.edu/values/ to learn more about our shared values. We seek scholars who will contribute to our community of teachers and researchers through excellence in innovative scholarship, engaged teaching, and participation in the intellectual life of the University. Boston University provides an environment where faculty and students work together across disciplines, perspectives, and experiences to advance knowledge and address society’s most pressing challenges. Required Skills Depending upon their level of experience, candidates should exhibit either potential for or evidence of excellence in teaching, a demonstrated ability or promising potential to successfully mentor and advise a wide range of students, and a demonstrated ability or potential to be a conscientious law school and university community member. We are interested in candidates who will bring an appreciation for ideological pluralism and an inclusive classroom environment. To Apply: Applicants should send a letter of interest and C.V./resume to lawappts@bu.edu. Boston University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualiﬁed applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, age, national origin, ethnicity, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law or identiﬁed in the University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination. Retaliation is also prohibited. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. Under Massachusetts law, we may not require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. Boston University, consistent with the AAU’s Principles on Preventing Sexual Harassment, conducts background checks for ﬁnal candidates for certain faculty and staff positions. As part of this process, we ask current and past employers of the last seven years whether there has been a substantiated ﬁnding of sexual misconduct under their policies. To move forward, ﬁnal candidates must complete and sign an “Authorization to Release Information” form after receiving an offer to enable this background check. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
    },
    "https://jobs.silkroad.com/BU/Faculty/jobs/317354": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Writing, Writing Program, College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Lecturer of Writing, Writing Program, College of Arts & Sciences - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Lecturer of Writing, Writing Program, College of Arts & Sciences - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Lecturer of Writing, Writing Program, College of Arts & Sciences ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937820929 Posted Date 9/29/2026 Minimum Salary $72,000.00 Maximum Salary $72,000.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Lecturer College of Arts & Sciences, Writing Program The College of Arts & Sciences Writing Program at Boston University expects to hire several full-time Lecturers in Writing to begin in July 2027. Responsibilities include teaching three classes per semester--theme-based first-year writing seminars and/or classes for multilingual writers--and participating in program service and ongoing professional development. The initial term of appointment is two years, with the possibility of renewal and promotion. The provisional starting salary is $72,000 (with a new contract currently under negotiation). Successful candidates will have the equivalent of at least five full-time years of experience teaching writing, will be flexible in the range of course levels they are prepared to teach, and will have experience in at least one of the following areas: science/social science writing, teaching writing to multilingual learners, teaching creativity/design thinking, teaching multimodal or oral communication. Successful candidates will also have expertise in inclusive pedagogy--including teaching writing in ways that equitably serve BU’s many multilingual students and in keeping with Writing Program values and the College ’s and University ’s social justice priorities. We are committed to building a diverse faculty and program, encompassing a breadth of perspectives, identities, and backgrounds that reflect those of BU’s racially and economically diverse undergraduate population . We strongly encourage candidates from historically marginalized groups to apply and are encouraged by BU’s redoubled efforts to recruit and retain underrepresented faculty in initiatives including the LGBTQIA+ Center for Faculty & Staff and its series of Faculty & Staff Community Networks . The Writing Program is an independent instructional unit with more than fifty full-time unionized Lecturers. We offer a two-semester sequence of theme-based writing seminars (18 students each) through which most BU undergraduates satisfy their writing requirements, and we prepare international undergraduate students for writing in their college classes through an additional two-course sequence for multilingual writers (15 students each). We also offer a small number of upper-level writing courses and a Minor in Writing . BU offers a rich range of resources for professional development and course enhancement. More information about the Arts & Sciences Writing Program is available at http://www.bu.edu/writingprogram/ and at https://www.bu.edu/teaching-writing/ . To apply Submit a letter of application (addressed to Dr. David Shawn, Chair of the Search Committee, College of Arts & Sciences Writing Program) and a curriculum vitae to Academic Jobs Online . Applications are due January 8, 2027. Those submitted via email or through a website other than Academic Jobs Online will not be considered. PLEASE DO NOT APPLY THROUGH THE BOSTON UNIVERSITY HR WEBSITE. Since its founding in 1839, Boston University has embraced a mission of openness and access, becoming one of the ﬁrst universities in the nation to welcome all students of ability regardless of race, gender, or creed. That tradition shapes our enduring commitment to academic freedom, free inquiry, and the robust exchange of ideas. Please visit https://www.bu.edu/values/ to learn more about our shared values. We seek scholars who will contribute to our community of teachers and researchers through excellence in innovative scholarship, engaged teaching, and participation in the intellectual life of the University. Boston University provides an environment where faculty and students work together across disciplines, perspectives, and experiences to advance knowledge and address society’s most pressing challenges. Boston University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualiﬁed applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, age, national origin, ethnicity, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law or identiﬁed in the University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination. Retaliation is also prohibited. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. Under Massachusetts law, we may not require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. Boston University, consistent with the AAU’s Principles on Preventing Sexual Harassment, conducts background checks for ﬁnal candidates for certain faculty and staff positions. As part of this process, we ask current and past employers of the last seven years whether there has been a substantiated ﬁnding of sexual misconduct under their policies. To move forward, ﬁnal candidates must complete and sign an “Authorization to Release Information” form after receiving an offer to enable this background check. DO NOT APPLY THROUGH THE BOSTON UNIVERSITY HR WEBSITE. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
