      "title": "Assistant Professor Faculty Position in the Department of Health Sciences, with a focus on Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health",
      "description": "Assistant Professor Faculty Position in the Department of Health Sciences, with a focus on Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Assistant Professor Faculty Position in the Department of Health Sciences, with a focus on Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Assistant Professor Faculty Position in the Department of Health Sciences, with a focus on Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599937911015 Posted Date 10/15/2026 Minimum Salary $100,000.00 Maximum Salary $115,000.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular The Department of Health Sciences at Boston University ’s Sargent College of Health & Rehabilitation Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in computational and cognitive neuroscienc e. We seek scholars working with clinical populations who integrate data-driven, biologically informed modeling and machine learning for neural decoding, bridging fundamental discoveries with clinical applications in sensorimotor and cognitive function and rehabilitation. T his position is part of BU’s major investment in convergent research , bringing together bold ideas, deep expertise , and perspectives from across disciplines to take on society’s most critical challenges. The position is part of a University -wide cluster hire in Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health, which builds on BU’s strength in Health Across the Lifespan . Spanning biology, biomedical engineering, electrical and computer engineering, health sciences, mathematics and statistics, and psychological and brain sciences, the cluster draws on BU’s strengths in neuroscience, engineering, computation, and AI to pursue transformative research questions, advance our understanding of neural information processing, and develop new approaches to neurological and psychiatric disease. The Department of Health Sciences is an interdisciplinary leader in research focused on improving health and well-being across diverse populations . The department offers undergraduate and graduate degree programs in Health Science, Human Physiology, Nutrition/Dietetics, and Public Health. Through hands-on learning, clinical partnerships, and specialized research labs, students are prepared for careers in medicine, neuroscience, public health, nutrition, and healthcare. The department has growing strengths in brain and cognitive health research across the lifespan. Faculty investigate the physiological, molecular, behavioral, social, environmental, and clinical factors that influence cognitive development, brain aging, dementia risk, mental health, rehabilitation, and quality of life . Research spans the full spectrum from fundamental to translational to clinical science, including molecular, cellular, and systems neuroscience and neuropathology, prevention science, health promotion, population health, implementation science, and health equity. The department welcomes scholars whose work seeks to uncover the basic biological mechanisms of brain health and disease, develop and test interventions to promote cognitive resilience and prevent cognitive decline, improve access to evidence-based care, and address disparities in brain health outcomes. Since its founding in 1839, Boston University has embraced a mission of openness and access, becoming one of the first universities in the nation to welcome all students of ability regardless of race, gender, or creed. That tradition shapes our enduring commitment to academic freedom, free inquiry, and the robust exchange of ideas. Please visit https://www.bu.edu/values/ to learn more about our shared values. We seek scholars who will contribute to our community of teachers and researchers through excellence in innovative scholarship , engaged teaching, and participation in the intellectual life of the University. Boston University provides an environment where faculty and students work together across disciplines, perspectives, and experiences to advance knowledge and address society’s most pressing challenges. Required Skills Position Qualifications Candidates should have a PhD or equivalent degree in Neuroscience, Health Sciences , or a related field, a demonstrated ability to obtain external funding to support their program of research and scholarship, and a commitment to excellence and innovation in teaching, education, and mentorship of students. Successful candidates will be expected to lead an independent research program; actively engage in collaborative research; teach and mentor students; and provide rank-appropriate service to the department, university, and profession. The salary allocated for these r oles is $1 0 0,000 to $ 115,000 . F inal salary determination and rank placement will be based on the candidate's academic record, research background, years of qualifying experience, and a variety of other factors, including but not limited to licenses, specialty, departmental budgets, training and internal pay comparison. The stated hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Application Requirements Applicants should provide a personal statement that describes the ir interest in both the convergent area of Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health and the department; curriculum vitae; a research statement describing their research interests and experience; and a teaching and mentoring statement detailing their approach to teaching and mentoring in an incl usive and diverse learning environment; and letters of recommendation from 3 references at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32917 Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, with a priority deadline of November 15. Applications will close November 30. Only applications submitted via the above AJO link will be reviewed. Boston University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender, age, national origin, ethnicity, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law or identified in the University’s Notice of Non-Discrimination. Retaliation is also prohibited. We are a VEVRAA Federal Contractor. Under Massachusetts law, we may not require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. Boston University, consistent with the AAU’s Principles on Preventing Sexual Harassment, conducts background checks for final candidates for certain faculty and staff positions. As part of this process, we ask current and past employers of the last seven years whether there has been a substantiated finding of sexual misconduct under their policies. To move forward, final candidates must complete and sign an “Authorization to Release Information” form after receiving an offer to enable this background check. This position is located in Boston, MA. View the Google Map in full screen . Apply close"
