ology tools in journalistic and civic settings . This position is part of BU’s major investment in convergent research, bringing together bold ideas, deep expertise , and perspectives from across disciplines to take on society’s most critical challenges. This is a tenure-track position. The position is part of a University -wide cluster hire in Livable and Resilient Cities, which builds on BU’s strength in Urban Development & Resilience . Spanning anthropology, biology, civic data science, environmental health, journalism, learning sciences, political science, sociology, and urban affairs, the cluster draws together BU’ s strengths in urban scholarship to advance new approaches to creating healthier, more equitable , and adaptable cities. The Department of Journalism at Boston University is a leader in innovative, public-facing communication focused on the critical role of information and storytelling in society. Situated within a major research university and a dynamic urban environment, the department offers an exceptional setting for scholars examining the social, political, environmental, and technological forces shaping contemporary cities. Faculty research and teaching engage topics including community engagement, media and democracy, public policy, data journalism, civic information ecosystems, and the communication of complex societal challenges. Since its founding in 1839, Boston University has embraced a mission of openness and access, becoming one of the first universities in the nation to welcome all students of ability regardless of race, gender, or creed. That tradition shapes our enduring commitment to academic freedom, free inquiry, and the robust exchange of ideas. Please visit https://www.bu.edu/values/ to learn more about our shared values. Boston University provides an environment where faculty and students work together across disciplines, perspectives, and experiences to advance knowledge and address society’s most pressing challenges. Required