      "title": "Convergent Faculty Search in Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health",
      "description": "Convergent Faculty Search in Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Convergent Faculty Search in Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health - Boston, Massachusetts, United States - Boston University Skip Navigation Menu Jobs My Account Loading... search chevron_left Boston University Jobs Apply Convergent Faculty Search in Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health ﻿ Category Charles River Campus --> Faculty Job Location Boston, Massachusetts, United States Tracking Code 26599938181023 Posted Date 10/23/2026 Minimum Salary $100,000.00 Maximum Salary $140,000.00 The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to departmental budgets, qualifications, experience, education, licenses, specialty, training and internal pay comparison. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. Position Type Full-Time/Regular Convergent Faculty Search in Advancing Brain and Cognitive Health Boston University is making a major investment in convergent research , bringing together bold ideas, deep expertise, and perspectives from across disciplines to take on society’s most critical challenges. With exceptional breadth across disciplines, a deeply collaborative research culture, and a strong history of interdisciplinary work, BU is uniquely positioned to pursue discoveries and solutions that no single field could achieve alone. At the heart of this investment is a cluster hiring program designed to strengthen connections across disciplines and build new areas of research excellence. BU is seeking intellectually fearless scholars who are eager to work across traditional boundaries—building new collaborations, opening new avenues of inquiry, advancing discoveries, and shaping new directions for research at BU. This cluster hire builds on BU’s strength in 